<BlueprintPage title="Depression Support and Assessment in Delhi NCR" description="Understand what a depression assessment may consider, including mood, daily functioning, health, safety and possible support." canonical="https://mindgracencr.in/depression-treatment-ncr" kicker="Depression and mood" answer="Depression-related concerns are best approached through a careful clinical assessment that considers mood, functioning, physical health, safety, and the person's goals." sections={[...sections,{title:'Planning a first consultation',paragraphs:['You can prepare by writing down what has changed, when it began, what daily activities are affected, what you have tried and what matters most to you now. Include current medicines and relevant health conditions if known. If it is difficult to speak freely, ask whether you may bring a trusted person or share a written note. You can ask about fees, appointment length, privacy and follow-up before booking.','A first visit is a conversation, not a commitment to a specific treatment. The clinician can explain their role, discuss options and answer questions. You may ask for clarification or more time to decide. If another kind of care seems more suitable, the clinician can discuss referral or coordination.','Depression can affect concentration, decision making, relationships, work, self-care and enjoyment. Some people describe sadness; others mainly notice emptiness, irritability, fatigue or withdrawal. Physical illness, medication effects, grief, stress and other mental health concerns can also shape these experiences. A clinician considers the whole pattern rather than relying on a single symptom.','Practical supports can sit alongside clinical care. A manageable daily routine, regular meals, gentle activity, social contact and a realistic sleep schedule may help some people maintain structure. Small steps are enough; low energy can make ordinary tasks feel demanding. Support should not frame depression as a lack of effort or suggest lifestyle changes alone are always sufficient.','If medication is discussed, ask what symptoms it is intended to address, how long it may take to review, what side effects to watch for and whom to contact with concerns. Do not start, stop or change prescribed medication without discussing it with the prescriber. If therapy is considered, ask what initial sessions will focus on and how progress will be reviewed.']}]} faq={faq} links={[{label:'Psychiatry',href:'/psychiatry'},{label:'Therapy',href:'/therapy'}]} />
